      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "improve(ui): friendlier panel load error state with reload prompt for stale chunks",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users hitting a lazy panel load failure in the Control UI (most commonly the stale-chunk \"Importing a module script failed\" error after a gateway update) would see a giant red callout stretched across the entire panel area, with the raw browser error message as the most prominent text. The state read as a crash rather than a routine, recoverable condition.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe router outlet rendered load failures as a bare `callout danger` with no layout styling, so the callout stretched to fill the routed pane. The raw exception text (\"Importing a module script failed.\") led the copy, and the common stale-chunk case (a background gateway update replacing hashed chunks) was presented identically to a genuine failure.\n\nThis change replaces it with a centered panel error state:\n\n- Icon, human title, and short subtitle; the raw error is demoted to a small muted mono line.\n- The stale-chunk case is presented as an update prompt (\"A new version is available\" with a Reload button, accent styling) instead of a red failure.\n- Generic load failures keep a danger-styled alert icon with a Retry button.\n\nRecovery behavior (revalidate vs. document-probe reload) is unchanged; only the presentation changed. The unused `lazyView.unknownError` key was dropped and copy trimmed so `ui/src/i18n/locales/en.ts` stays within the TypeScript LOC ratchet.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAnyone using the Control UI when a panel chunk fails to load — most visibly right after a gateway update. They now get a clear, calm explanation and an obvious Reload/Retry action instead of a full-pane red error box.\n\nStale-chunk prompt (after gateway update):\n\n![stale chunk update prompt](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/lazy-view-error/lazy-error-stale.png)\n\nGeneric load failure:\n\n![generic load failure](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/lazy-view-error/lazy-error-generic.png)\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Screenshots above captured live against `pnpm dev:ui:mock` with route imports forced to reject (WebKit stale-chunk message and a generic HTTP 500 message).\n- `ui/src/app/router-outlet.test.ts` updated: the stale-chunk test now asserts the update-prompt copy; existing assertions for the raw error text, retry-through-latest-context, and offline fallback behavior still pass.\n- `pnpm check:changed` (coreTests + ui lanes) green on Blacksmith Testbox, including the TypeScript LOC ratchet.\n- Codex autoreview run on the branch diff.\n",
        "branch": "claude/error-handling-improvements-57f7ee",
